<p>Regarding your first point: it certainly could be that the device only reshapes what we see, but I would think that the tachyon emission constrains that possibility somewhat. If you wanted to alter EM waves there are more efficient ways to do that, and tachyons are tied in sci-fi narrative to time shenanigans.</p>
<p>Regarding your second point: of course the aliens aren't all going to be able to uniquely identify us from this SCP, which is why we haven't already started looking for a way to undo it. But the SCP does leave a lot of clues which, taken together, help to identify us - maps of the solar system, of the solar neighborhood, of the Milky Way.</p>

