					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="1361261"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1397115400 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 Apr 2014 07:36</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2009895">
									

<p>This exceeds my personal Conservation of WTF threshold by a huge margin. Leaving aside the absolute ridiculousness of the containment procedures, which would pretty much guarantee that this information gets leaked, assuming that no amateur astronomers would notice entire galaxy clusters arranged in the described manner, this is just too much.</p>
<p>This essentially requires the creators of this skip to be God, and I have a hard time believing that something that's attained that much power is going to use it for such a completely asinine purpose. And then mysteriously vanish, leaving the God Box buried in a hole somewhere for some reason. And then of course the Foundation deems the wisest course of action to be fucking with the thing that causes retrocausal readjustment of the entire goddamn universe. Nope.</p>
<p>Also, my impression is that we're supposed to take this article seriously. If that's the case&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rough translations of messages include &quot;WE ARE KINGS&quot;, &quot;WE ARE SPECIAL&quot;, and &quot;WE ARE THE CENTER&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Jesus, really? These guys attain the goddamn power to change the SKY and that's what they come up with? Are they going to come back and carve &quot;LOL EAT AT JOE'S&quot; into the moon?</p>
<p>There's the elements of something really good here, but it's weighed down by just way too much ridiculousness.</p>

							</div>

								
					
